\begin{align*}
    a^2 + b^2 &= 7^2 \\
    b^2 &= 49 - a^2 \, .
   \end{align*}
Next, we can use the fact that the hyperbola passes through the point $(2, 12)$ to find a relationship between $a$ and $b$. Substituting this point into the equation of the hyperbola, we get
\begin{align*}
    \frac{2^2}{a^2} - \frac{12^2}{b^2} &= 1 \\
    \frac{4}{a^2} - \frac{144}{b^2} &= 1 \, .
   \end{align*}
Substituting $b^2 = 49 - a^2$ into this equation gives
\begin{align*}
    \frac{4}{a^2} - \frac{144}{49 - a^2} &= 1 \, .
   \end{align*}
